WEBVTT

00:09.160 --> 00:10.740
Hey, you...

00:11.370 --> 00:12.340
Romantica!

00:12.340 --> 00:13.210
You're safe—

00:15.330 --> 00:18.030
How do you know my name?

00:18.030 --> 00:20.230
Have we met before?

00:24.590 --> 00:26.170
Oh, sorry...

00:26.720 --> 00:29.000
I, uh, saw that.

00:33.510 --> 00:35.220
Hmm.

00:35.220 --> 00:38.260
So we're in the same testing group.

00:38.780 --> 00:41.390
Best of luck to you, I guess.

00:48.440 --> 00:50.480
<i>Of course I know you.</i>

00:52.500 --> 00:57.710
<i>You have no idea how 
devastated I was to lose you.</i>

00:59.080 --> 01:04.780
<i>I will never let you go through 
such an ordeal ever again!</i>

01:20.810 --> 01:27.980
<i>Fate is always more heroic than any story</i>

01:30.350 --> 01:37.130
<i>The one and only despair flaunts 
a completely different sky</i>

01:37.130 --> 01:39.700
<i>A stolen smile</i>

01:39.700 --> 01:49.080
<i>Put a period on the nights 
of lament and depression</i>

01:49.080 --> 01:53.710
<i>When the season comes around 
for the second time, gear yourself up</i>

01:53.710 --> 01:58.130
<i>For the final challenge</i>

01:58.130 --> 02:01.560
<i>Why don't we struggle, cry, and bloom away?</i>

02:01.560 --> 02:07.760
<i>I have a future, a future I want to 
go back to no matter what it takes</i>

02:07.760 --> 02:11.100
<i>Here we go and embrace 
the next life, nice to meet you</i>

02:11.100 --> 02:18.150
<i>There's a world, a world 
I want to repaint with you</i>

02:18.150 --> 02:20.480
<i>Let's go see the end together</i>

02:20.480 --> 02:23.120
<i>The ending credits signal the beginning</i>

02:23.120 --> 02:27.960
<i>A special story drawn by light and shadow</i>

02:27.960 --> 02:30.290
<i>Ge ge ge ge ge get back</i>

02:30.290 --> 02:32.920
<i>To my own story</i>

02:37.550 --> 02:42.140
<b>  The Test</b>

02:37.550 --> 02:42.140
<b></b>Episode 2

02:42.390 --> 02:45.090
Desir, you're in Group D.

02:45.660 --> 02:47.650
The test is...

02:48.310 --> 02:52.520
a race in the Erenstee Plains in the 
beginner level of the Shadow World.

02:54.200 --> 02:55.760
But don't worry.

02:55.760 --> 02:58.460
We call it a Shadow World, 
but it's not dangerous.

02:58.460 --> 03:00.170
It's actually safe.

03:01.020 --> 03:05.980
The Shadow Worlds used at Hebrion Academy 
are created for the purpose of the tests.

03:07.300 --> 03:10.280
They employ a safety system,

03:10.280 --> 03:14.800
so even if you receive fatal damage, 
you can evacuate immediately.

03:15.440 --> 03:17.020
Damage...

03:17.020 --> 03:19.440
Right. In other words, in this test—

03:19.440 --> 03:24.880
The use of magic and attacks towards 
other participants is allowed.

03:24.880 --> 03:26.440
You know?

03:26.440 --> 03:27.940
Elheim!

03:28.740 --> 03:34.450
And... it is impossible 
for you lot to pass the test.

03:34.960 --> 03:37.780
You won't know that until we try!

03:37.780 --> 03:40.490
Oh, but I do.

03:41.560 --> 03:46.880
Allow me to present my mentee,
 Azest Kingscrown.

03:47.220 --> 03:48.750
She's a magic knight.

03:49.870 --> 03:51.550
A magic knight?!

03:52.220 --> 03:53.490
Azest...

03:54.880 --> 03:56.840
<i>I know you very well.</i>

03:58.390 --> 04:01.460
<i>She is a magic knight of ice 
 and a high Circle mage</i>

04:01.460 --> 04:05.100
<i>who can wield vision magic, 
which is impossible to inverse.</i>

04:05.100 --> 04:07.190
<i>And she's better with a sword 
than most pure knights.</i>

04:07.640 --> 04:09.670
<i>She'll be my most reliable teammate.</i>

04:17.640 --> 04:20.530
<i>I guess she's still not much of a talker.</i>

04:25.790 --> 04:27.760
What's the matter, Ladoria?

04:27.760 --> 04:30.500
Have you lost your steam from earlier already?

04:30.970 --> 04:34.040
Oh, please! You just got lucky 
with your mentee assignment!

04:34.040 --> 04:35.800
It doesn't reflect your skills whatsoever!

04:36.440 --> 04:40.070
No, it obviously reflects my personal virtue.

04:40.070 --> 04:43.950
I guess a commoner is a perfect 
fit for someone of your level.

04:46.180 --> 04:48.690
What did you say?!

04:51.500 --> 04:54.050
<i>Good to see you again, Azest.</i>

04:55.900 --> 04:59.820
I mean... Frankly, your odds aren't 
that great against a magic knight.

05:00.260 --> 05:03.030
But don't give up, okay?

05:03.690 --> 05:06.300
Thank you, Ladoria.

05:07.100 --> 05:10.790
<i>We will now begin the testing for Group D.</i>

05:10.790 --> 05:13.990
<i>Participants, please assemble at the gate.</i>

05:14.830 --> 05:16.050
I'm off.

05:16.950 --> 05:18.210
Good luck!

05:58.530 --> 06:02.070
<i>Welcome to Erenstee Plains 
in the Shadow World.</i>

06:04.060 --> 06:08.930
<i>You will be aiming for the goal over there.</i>

06:09.740 --> 06:13.110
<i>Only the top three will pass the test.</i>

06:13.110 --> 06:18.940
<i>You are allowed to use magic attacks, 
interference, and any other methods.</i>

06:19.600 --> 06:25.100
<i>If you receive fatal damage,
 you will be disqualified.</i>

06:27.120 --> 06:28.950
<i>Please line up at the starting line.</i>

06:35.960 --> 06:38.670
<i>Azest survived until the end, like I did.</i>

06:39.400 --> 06:43.650
<i>Did she come back to this world 
with past memories, by any chance?</i>

06:45.280 --> 06:49.930
<i>I have no idea what she's thinking... 
not that I could ever tell before.</i>

06:50.450 --> 06:52.060
Desir Herrman.

06:53.060 --> 06:55.360
H-How do you know my name?!

06:56.400 --> 06:59.010
I checked the roster before I came here.

07:00.680 --> 07:02.950
Oh, I see.

07:03.300 --> 07:07.780
You are at the lowest Circle, 
with below average physical abilities.

07:07.780 --> 07:11.330
Even if you continue training, 
you have no future.

07:12.300 --> 07:14.160
You may be right.

07:14.860 --> 07:17.580
<i>Sounds like she has no past memories...</i>

07:17.940 --> 07:22.310
I noticed that you've been observing me, 
but you need not be wary.

07:22.960 --> 07:25.840
I have no interest in attacking the weak.

07:26.800 --> 07:28.020
Is that so?

07:28.020 --> 07:29.030
Thanks.

07:31.980 --> 07:37.580
<i>The race through Erenstee Plains 
will now begin.</i>

07:37.580 --> 07:41.080
<i>Counting down. Five, four,</i>

07:41.500 --> 07:45.090
<i>three, two, one,</i>

07:45.090 --> 07:46.210
<i>start!</i>

07:49.280 --> 07:50.440
Hey!

07:50.440 --> 07:52.260
You're kicking up the dust!

07:53.420 --> 07:54.500
Jeez!

08:01.420 --> 08:03.960
Oh, I'm sorry!

08:07.440 --> 08:10.640
It's fluffy... So cute!

08:12.160 --> 08:14.840
You still like that sort of stuff.

08:15.210 --> 08:18.040
Huh?! What do you mean by "still"?!

08:18.040 --> 08:20.610
What do you think you know about me?!

08:21.180 --> 08:22.650
Um...

08:22.650 --> 08:25.260
What? Are you, like, hitting on me?!

08:25.260 --> 08:26.640
You think you're hitting on me?!

08:26.640 --> 08:28.990
Why don't you focus on the race?

08:29.730 --> 08:31.320
You're right.

08:31.320 --> 08:35.750
But at this rate, both of us 
are going to be disqualified.

08:35.750 --> 08:38.110
Don't lump me in with you.

08:38.110 --> 08:39.750
Stop acting so familiar!

08:40.240 --> 08:41.710
Sorry, my bad.

08:41.710 --> 08:42.880
My gosh!

08:42.880 --> 08:45.850
That face you're making really 
bugs me, so stop it!

08:46.100 --> 08:48.920
I just missed this so much, I can't help it.

08:48.920 --> 08:50.640
You missed <i>what</i> exactly?!

09:02.900 --> 09:05.700
Man, stop sticking your nose 
 where it doesn't belong!

09:05.700 --> 09:07.650
I'll blast you away first!

09:09.900 --> 09:11.550
Fire Rod!

09:15.480 --> 09:17.250
Wind Strike!

09:29.900 --> 09:36.150
<i>Due to fatal damage, Sing Eggs is 
 disqualified from the Shadow World.</i>

09:36.510 --> 09:38.910
<i>There are five participants remaining.</i>

09:41.220 --> 09:43.490
I guess I owe you one.

09:44.220 --> 09:46.530
Thank you for looking out for me.

09:47.240 --> 09:48.820
However!

09:48.820 --> 09:52.240
This settles the score, you hear me?!

09:52.580 --> 09:53.660
Sure.

09:53.660 --> 09:56.180
I. Told. You!

09:56.180 --> 09:58.710
Stop making that face!

10:01.530 --> 10:03.150
But don't you need to catch up?

10:03.150 --> 10:05.090
They've got quite a lead.

10:05.090 --> 10:06.090
Hmph!

10:07.140 --> 10:10.350
I was going to save this for later, but...

10:10.350 --> 10:11.880
I guess it's fine.

10:13.420 --> 10:16.250
I'll show you my true abilities.

10:16.620 --> 10:18.860
Aerosweep!

10:22.870 --> 10:25.770
Groups A and C have just finished.

10:26.370 --> 10:29.230
Groups D and F are currently being tested.

10:29.780 --> 10:31.950
Everything is going smoothly.

10:32.900 --> 10:36.270
This year's candidates are excellent.

10:36.270 --> 10:37.340
Indeed.

10:37.340 --> 10:41.120
After all, we have a magic knight this year.

10:41.120 --> 10:43.180
Overwhelmingly strong.

10:43.180 --> 10:45.380
She's what all nobles should be.

10:45.760 --> 10:47.550
Exactly.

10:47.550 --> 10:52.300
By the way, there is a commoner in Group D.

10:54.210 --> 10:56.920
In the same group as 
the magic knight, of all things?

10:56.920 --> 10:58.470
Even I pity him.

11:14.810 --> 11:16.340
<i>So fast.</i>

11:16.340 --> 11:18.830
<i>As expected of the magic knight.</i>

11:18.830 --> 11:22.190
<i>Well, if I keep up this pace, I should pass.</i>

11:35.920 --> 11:39.930
A blast like this isn't strong 
enough to blow me away...

11:40.360 --> 11:41.640
What?!

11:42.470 --> 11:45.490
She's cutting through... the wind?!

11:46.690 --> 11:48.790
That's a magic knight for you.

11:48.790 --> 11:50.320
Just you watch!

11:57.450 --> 11:58.500
Wait...

12:00.920 --> 12:03.080
What the heck?!

12:05.240 --> 12:10.690
<i>Due to fatal damage, 
Treviri Tycus and Nasi Holm</i>

12:10.690 --> 12:13.470
<i>are disqualified from the Shadow World.</i>

12:15.680 --> 12:18.510
<i>There are three participants remaining.</i>

12:20.120 --> 12:22.010
I guess one of them survived.

12:23.020 --> 12:26.370
Anyhow, now both of us will pass.

12:27.270 --> 12:30.520
Did you really think I'd say that?

12:31.810 --> 12:34.030
You're next.

12:40.600 --> 12:43.040
You'd better drop out.

12:43.710 --> 12:45.420
May I ask why?

12:45.420 --> 12:47.690
That! That face you're making!

12:47.690 --> 12:49.670
It pisses me off!

12:49.670 --> 12:53.020
Is that the reason? 
Isn't that a little harsh?

12:53.020 --> 12:55.850
Oh, not at all.

12:56.330 --> 13:01.080
I'm trying to talk you out of this 
before you get hurt.

13:01.080 --> 13:03.480
Aren't I so kind?

13:05.960 --> 13:10.960
If you get it, go ahead and drop out now.

13:10.960 --> 13:12.200
Okay?

13:14.230 --> 13:15.270
I refuse.

13:17.250 --> 13:19.240
Good, nice to know you're obedient—

13:19.690 --> 13:21.960
Wait! What did you just say?!

13:22.710 --> 13:24.960
I said I refuse.

13:25.350 --> 13:26.940
Are you stupid?

13:26.940 --> 13:28.940
You saw my magic, didn't you?!

13:30.030 --> 13:31.300
Stop smiling!

13:31.970 --> 13:35.330
I gave you a chance...

13:35.330 --> 13:37.080
I'm through with you!

13:47.150 --> 13:49.460
It'll hurt so bad you'll think you're gonna die,

13:49.460 --> 13:52.530
but they say you can't die here, so rest easy.

13:53.590 --> 13:55.360
Wind Strike!

14:05.100 --> 14:06.640
Bye-bye!

14:12.150 --> 14:14.770
You're able to handle 
that many simultaneously?

14:14.770 --> 14:16.020
Impressive.

14:17.570 --> 14:19.260
As expected of you, Romantica.

14:21.080 --> 14:22.080
Huh?!

14:22.800 --> 14:26.810
But you prioritize speed, 
so your control is weak.

14:28.470 --> 14:31.610
A slight adjustment to the trajectory, 
and it won't hit.

14:32.140 --> 14:34.410
Wha... Who do you think you are?!

14:34.410 --> 14:36.680
It just happened to miss, that's all!

14:37.560 --> 14:39.890
There's no way you could beat me!

14:41.460 --> 14:43.340
I won't miss this time.

14:46.570 --> 14:49.900
Have a taste of my Venom Wind!

14:51.780 --> 14:53.120
Same thing again.

14:53.570 --> 14:55.770
If I change the air currents a little...

14:58.430 --> 15:00.200
They'll miss the target.

15:02.210 --> 15:03.470
Did you just...?

15:04.250 --> 15:05.400
No way...

15:07.100 --> 15:09.020
An inversing spell?

15:10.570 --> 15:11.980
Correct.

15:13.790 --> 15:14.820
No way...

15:16.260 --> 15:21.100
<i>Usually, someone has to be at a much higher 
Circle to be able to inverse your spell.</i>

15:22.030 --> 15:26.330
That's impossible, 
since you're at the lowest Circle!

15:36.090 --> 15:37.180
Are you serious?

15:39.450 --> 15:41.080
I can't believe it...

15:41.830 --> 15:44.310
He really did inverse it.

15:45.340 --> 15:51.310
<i>Does that mean his skills 
are much higher than mine?</i>

15:52.600 --> 15:54.400
Shall we finish this up?

15:56.910 --> 15:59.980
I have others I need to defeat.

16:00.420 --> 16:02.950
I can't stay here for long.

16:07.630 --> 16:09.290
So what?

16:10.020 --> 16:14.000
Try and see if you can 
inverse this many spells!

16:26.950 --> 16:29.400
<i>You are strong, Romantica.</i>

16:29.990 --> 16:32.980
<i>Surely one of the best among 
this year's new students.</i>

16:34.150 --> 16:36.600
<i>But not strong enough.</i>

16:37.440 --> 16:40.450
<i>At this rate, we will 
repeat the same future.</i>

16:41.170 --> 16:44.860
<i>Romantica, you can become stronger.</i>

16:45.620 --> 16:49.470
<i>And that's why I have to 
be the one to win now.</i>

17:09.710 --> 17:12.310
There are three things you overlooked.

17:14.400 --> 17:18.210
First, inversing spells 
isn't the only thing I can do.

17:18.210 --> 17:19.400
Grease.

17:23.590 --> 17:26.510
That's one of the basic spells 
to erase friction.

17:27.210 --> 17:29.370
Why would you use that?

17:30.250 --> 17:34.020
Second, you're not the one 
I've been fighting all along.

17:35.450 --> 17:41.020
Third, we're not being tested on magic skills, 
but on whether or not we can reach the goal.

17:43.710 --> 17:48.130
And even if we receive fatal 
damage here, we won't die.

17:48.510 --> 17:50.490
Which means I can do something like this.

17:53.260 --> 17:55.960
That's... fire magic?

17:56.470 --> 17:57.770
Are you insane?!

17:57.770 --> 18:00.020
You might not die, 
but you'll still take damage!

18:00.020 --> 18:01.360
Fireball.

18:11.690 --> 18:13.340
Whoa.

18:13.830 --> 18:16.880
He's really out there.

18:40.730 --> 18:42.140
He'll catch up with me.

18:44.200 --> 18:47.280
I don't know what kind of method 
you used to beat Romantica Eru,

18:47.670 --> 18:49.680
but I will take back that I called you weak.

18:51.630 --> 18:53.290
I'll defeat you with everything I've got.

18:57.740 --> 18:59.920
Magic Arrows of Prey.

19:10.630 --> 19:13.720
Analysis completed on every linked spell.

19:15.070 --> 19:18.100
Control obtained over Magic Arrows of Prey.

19:20.660 --> 19:21.730
<i>Inversing the spell?</i>

19:22.610 --> 19:26.650
<i>I'll end this before you take them all!</i>

19:30.580 --> 19:31.780
Adjusting trajectory!

19:46.410 --> 19:48.170
You dodged the fatal blow.

19:54.930 --> 19:59.310
Inversing spells... 
so that's how you defeated her.

20:05.320 --> 20:07.460
I won't give you time to inverse my spell.

20:09.970 --> 20:12.110
I'll crush you in one fell swoop!

20:14.810 --> 20:16.170
Good call.

20:16.530 --> 20:17.920
As expected from you.

20:24.520 --> 20:25.780
Adjusting trajectory!

20:35.450 --> 20:36.970
<i>He's using the blowback...?!</i>

20:39.540 --> 20:42.910
You're too hung up on beating me, Azest.

20:50.820 --> 20:54.320
<i>First place in Group D is Desir Herrman!</i>

21:10.370 --> 21:11.390
<i>Azest...</i>

21:13.710 --> 21:14.820
<i>Romantica...</i>

21:17.850 --> 21:21.000
<i>We have to get stronger</i>

21:23.390 --> 21:25.900
<i>so we can overcome that tragedy.</i>

21:32.770 --> 21:35.520
<i>I thought you were the only one for me</i>

21:35.520 --> 21:38.230
<i>I thought you were the only one for me</i>

21:38.230 --> 21:41.840
<i>Even though that couldn't be</i>

21:46.320 --> 21:51.730
<i>All emotions will fade away sooner or later</i>

21:51.730 --> 21:56.330
<i>So we can pretend it's all a fairytale</i>

21:57.080 --> 22:02.450
<i>Even love is just a fleeting dream</i>

22:02.450 --> 22:06.880
<i>So let's throw the dice 
and see what's in store</i>

22:07.230 --> 22:13.400
<i>I rolled a six today, eight times in a row</i>

22:13.400 --> 22:18.660
<i>But who knows what 
tomorrow's play will bring?</i>

22:18.660 --> 22:23.690
<i>I hope one day we'll be able to say</i>

22:23.690 --> 22:27.900
<i>That not knowing was the best part</i>

22:29.410 --> 22:32.180
<i>I thought you were the only one for me</i>

22:32.180 --> 22:34.870
<i>I thought you were the only one for me</i>

22:34.870 --> 22:38.380
<i>Even though that couldn't be</i>

22:40.250 --> 22:43.090
<i>If we happen to meet again in the next life</i>

22:43.090 --> 22:45.670
<i>I'll take any help I can get, 
even my own cat's</i>

22:45.670 --> 22:48.380
<i>Because this time</i>

22:48.380 --> 22:52.510
<i>I'll roll a three</i>

23:12.530 --> 23:13.940
<i>Time's up!</i>

23:13.940 --> 23:17.070
<i>Group F's qualifier is Doneta Hadoon!</i>

23:35.520 --> 23:40.030
<b>    Comrades</b>

23:35.520 --> 23:40.030
<b></b>Episode 3

23:36.170 --> 23:38.520
Next episode, "Comrades."
